WEBVTT

00:00:04.099 --> 00:00:09.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me? Right, Thursday the twelfth. Let's get through the board.</v>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:18.519
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, loud and clear. Unlike the broken coffee machine in the canteen. That's just making a sort of angry bubbling noise now.</v>

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.750
<v Jamie Brennan>Still better conversation than you before your first coffee.</v>

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:32.009
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Cheers. Also, whose new car is that in the car park? Very brave, parking something that shiny next to this place.</v>

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.399
<v Fiona Doyle>Not mine. Mine's the one with half the county stuck to the wheel arches.</v>

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:51.340
<v Aisha Begum>Never mind the car, the heating in the portakabin's either tropical or completely off. I'm sat here in my coat. Just having a moan, before that goes on the board.</v>

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Mine's still on too. Teams makes it look like we're meeting outdoors.</v>

00:00:58.369 --> 00:01:01.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we become the weather report—finished work first.</v>

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:10.319
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the Gas Turbine 1 last night. That's done, not something rolling into today.</v>

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that one's closed.</v>

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:22.010
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I signed off the inspection on the line three on Tuesday. Still showing in the old notes, but it's finished.</v>

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:31.079
<v Fiona Doyle>Same with line two. Tested the line two yesterday and it's all fine now. Nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:01:33.519 --> 00:01:38.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Those are history, then. Anything else we need to understand before the actual jobs?</v>

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:49.469
<v Priya Raman>Um, I saw the pressure on the turbine one gas valve dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own. Just an observation.</v>

00:01:51.489 --> 00:01:54.640
<v Olumide Adeyemi>It settled again, did it? Not still sitting low?</v>

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.299
<v Priya Raman>No, back where it was. I'm not raising a separate job off that here.</v>

00:02:03.099 --> 00:02:10.449
<v Priya Raman>The existing HV switchboard work is still blocked, though. Can't get to the HV switchboard until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:19.680
<v Priya Raman>And I can't get to the Site Water System until production gives us a window either. Same access problem, both still waiting.</v>

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Both remain blocked, not fresh commitments for today.</v>

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.210
<v Sarah Okafor>What about the purchase order for the feedwater pump? That still needs chasing, doesn't it?</v>

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.719
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the feedwater pump by the 28th. It's fairly important.</v>

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:44.719
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, the order chase, rather than saying the pump itself will be here by then.</v>

00:02:47.039 --> 00:02:50.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Aisha has the chase, by the 28th. Fairly important.</v>

00:02:50.900 --> 00:03:00.699
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll sort the training records for the new starters by end of day. No rush on that one; it doesn't need to jump ahead of the plant jobs.</v>

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, Saz for the training records. End of day, no rush.</v>

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:09.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. That's mine.</v>

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:18.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi, can you go to Harbour Road to pick up the replacement parts for the line 1 hydraulics today at 2pm? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:27.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll go to Harbour Road and pick up the replacement parts for the line 1 hydraulics. Today at 2pm works.</v>

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.919
<v Jamie Brennan>Just the collection we're talking about, yeah? Not fitting them as part of that.</v>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Just collection. Normal priority, today at 2pm. Got it.</v>

00:03:38.759 --> 00:03:45.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha Begum, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the turbine two water valve today at 2pm? It's urgent.</v>

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:53.310
<v Aisha Begum>Yes, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the turbine two water valve today at 2pm. Understood, it's urgent.</v>

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.900
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—the turbine two water valve, not the gas valve we just mentioned?</v>

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:05.020
<v Aisha Begum>That's right, turbine two water valve. Separate job from that pressure observation.</v>

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:12.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Olu, can you check the guarding on the Main Outfeed Conveyor? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:18.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the Main Outfeed Conveyor. Got that.</v>

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.910
<v Tomasz Nowak>Guarding check only, as it's written there?</v>

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:30.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, checking the guarding. Not signing myself up for a load of alterations off the back of this call.</v>

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:37.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. It matters but it's not urgent, and there's no deadline attached to that one.</v>

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:47.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser this afternoon? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:57.459
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser this afternoon. Properly isolated for the jam clearance, obviously.</v>

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:04.399
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The sensor check's included as well, then? Not just getting the trapped bit out.</v>

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:12.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, both. Clear the jam and check the sensors, not just pull it out and call it done.</v>

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:18.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. This afternoon, Tomasz. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:20.839 --> 00:05:25.040
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you inspect the main water valve for leaks by Wednesday?</v>

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.779
<v Priya Raman>Yes, I'll inspect the main water valve for leaks by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:30.199 --> 00:05:38.250
<v Priya Raman>And just to keep the notes straight, that's the main water valve inspection, separate from the blocked Site Water System work I mentioned.</v>

00:05:40.129 --> 00:05:43.980
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, separate entries. We're not treating the blocked work as released.</v>

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:54.709
<v Fiona Doyle>One without a name against it: someone needs to do a site visit at Tollgate Water Treatment Works with the contractor tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:05:55.939 --> 00:06:02.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, no rush on that one in priority terms, but the visit is tomorrow at 9:30. Anyone taking it?</v>

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:09.209
<v Jamie Brennan>I'm not putting my name against that. Don't count me as covering it.</v>

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.910
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, I'm not volunteering for that one either.</v>

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:22.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay... nobody's taken the site visit at Tollgate Water Treatment Works. It needs doing, but it stays unowned. No rush, tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:06:23.019 --> 00:06:26.870
<v Fiona Doyle>Fine. Blank owner, then. Raising it wasn't me offering to go.</v>

00:06:27.439 --> 00:06:31.639
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Dangerous pause, that. In these meetings a pause normally means you've volunteered.</v>

00:06:32.019 --> 00:06:34.819
<v Aisha Begum>Or your Teams has frozen. Equally binding, apparently.</v>

00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:41.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Not on my board. Right, quick check that I've not mangled anyone's commitments.</v>

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:48.699
<v Fiona Doyle>Mine's the Harbour Road pickup for the line 1 hydraulics, today at 2pm, normal priority. That's right.</v>

00:06:50.339 --> 00:06:59.439
<v Aisha Begum>Both mine are right: the urgent turbine two water valve sign-off today at 2pm, and the fairly important feedwater pump purchase order chase by the 28th.</v>

00:07:01.459 --> 00:07:07.060
<v Priya Raman>And mine's the main water valve leak inspection by Wednesday. The access blockers are still blockers.</v>

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:12.279
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Guarding on the Main Outfeed Conveyor for me. Matters, not urgent. All good.</v>

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:20.160
<v Tomasz Nowak>Palletiser jam and sensors this afternoon for me. Not an emergency, but won't let it slip.</v>

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:28.439
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll sort the new starters' training records by end of day, no rush. That's everything agreed.</v>

00:07:30.269 --> 00:07:36.220
<v Sarah Okafor>The contractor visit remains unowned, just so there's no assumption someone's silently picked it up. Thanks, everyone.</v>
